    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on a high-upside slate today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (80.76) and **Kyle Tucker** (77.97). **Gunnar Henderson** is our primary anchor against Michael McGreevy, benefiting from an elite SP skill boost (+11%) and a massive dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) that positions him as the most potent bat in the order. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** thrives against the high xERA of AJ Smith-Shawver (5.23), with his score inflated by a 19% SP skill advantage. Rounding out our elite tier, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.27) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) both draw favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs near 4.80, with **Jackson Merrill** specifically seeing his stock rise significantly due to a +19% SP skill correction.\n\nOur strategy for maximizing stolen bases remains aggressive, even with some marginal starts. While **Nasim Nunez** (56.21) sits at the bottom of the order, he remains a necessary inclusion; his speed profile, combined with the \"Slow SP Delivery\" bonus (+4%), makes him a vital catalyst for our SB category. The most difficult bench decision involved **Coby Mayo** (50.55), who narrowly missed the cut. While he offers power, his lack of stolen base utility and a lower score compared to the bottom of our current outfield rotation pushed him to the bench. We are also monitoring **Luis Robert Jr.** (46.20), whose score was dragged down by a poor platoon matchup against Dustin May, forcing us to prioritize safer, high-efficiency options like **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.41), who is enjoying a breakout day profile against Peter Lambert.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in our \"Lineup Pending\" designations; while we have forecasted based on historical usage, any late-scratch or order fluctuation for **Drake Baldwin** or **Miguel Vargas** could alter their efficiency scores. **Miguel Vargas** carries a specific situational edge today\u2014wind blowing out (+5%)\u2014which, when paired with the slow delivery of MacKenzie Gore, gives him a sneaky upside despite a sub-elite xERA opponent. We remain cautious of **Dominic Smith** (50.04), whose score is hovering near our floor due to his placement in the 7-hole, though he serves as a placeholder to maintain our game cap strategy. With **Andy Pages** still sidelined on the IL, our current depth must carry the load to maintain our 5x5 standing.",
